					</summary>
					<p class="font-body" style="margin-top: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 1rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-blue); font-size: 1.05rem;">
						Click the <strong>"📝 Export Word (.doc)"</strong> or <strong>"🖨️ Export PDF / Print"</strong> button in the dashboard. The tool exports a clean fitting card with your bust, waist, hips, body silhouette, and designer adjustments ready to hand to your consultant.
					</p>
				</details>

				<details class="faq-accordion" style="margin-bottom: 1rem; border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.75rem; background: var(--bg-paper);">
					<summary class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.2rem; cursor: pointer; color: var(--accent-blue);">
						Do I need to wear shoes or heels when measuring?
					</summary>
					<p class="font-body" style="margin-top: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 1rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-blue); font-size: 1.05rem;">
						Shoes do not affect your bust, waist, or hip size. However, you will need your exact wedding shoes or identical heel height during your first alteration fitting to establish the floor-length hemline and bustle points.
					</p>
				</details>

				<details class="faq-accordion" style="margin-bottom: 1rem; border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.75rem; background: var(--bg-paper);">
					<summary class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.2rem; cursor: pointer; color: var(--accent-blue);">
						What is "Split Sizing" and when should I request it?
					</summary>
					<p class="font-body" style="margin-top: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 1rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-blue); font-size: 1.05rem;">
						Split sizing occurs when a designer agrees to cut the bodice in one size (e.g. Size 6) and the skirt in another (e.g. Size 12) before sewing them together. This typically incurs a $200-$400 custom charge from the manufacturer, but can save significantly on post-delivery alteration costs for dramatic pear or hourglass figures.
					</p>
				</details>

				<details class="faq-accordion" style="margin-bottom: 1rem; border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.75rem; background: var(--bg-paper);">
					<summary class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.2rem; cursor: pointer; color: var(--accent-blue);">
						How does fabric type affect how a wedding dress fits?
					</summary>
					<p class="font-body" style="margin-top: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 1rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-blue); font-size: 1.05rem;">
						Stiff fabrics like Mikado, Duchess Satin, and Brocade have zero give—requiring exact millimeter precision in measurements. Lightweight fabrics like Crepe, Chiffon, or Stretch Jersey offer gentle give and drape more forgivingly across the hips and thighs.
					</p>
				</details>
			</section>

		</article>

	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	.unit-toggle-btn {
		background: #fff;
		border: none;
		padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem;
		font-family: var(--font-heading);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		cursor: pointer;
		color: var(--fg-pencil);
		transition: background 0.15s ease;
	}
	.unit-toggle-btn.active-unit {
		background: var(--fg-pencil);
		color: #fff;
	}

	.preset-meas-btn {
		background: #fff;
		border: 1px solid var(--fg-pencil);
		border-radius: 3px;
		padding: 0.2rem 0.45rem;
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		cursor: pointer;
		font-family: var(--font-body);
	}
	.preset-meas-btn:hover {
		background: var(--muted-paper);
	}

	.silhouette-card {
		background: var(--bg-paper);
		border: 1.5px solid var(--fg-pencil);
		border-radius: 4px;
		padding: 0.85rem;
	}
	.silhouette-card h5 {
		margin: 0 0 0.25rem 0;
		font-family: var(--font-heading);
		font-size: 1rem;
		color: var(--accent-blue);
	}

	.print-only {
		display: none;
	}

	@media print {
		body * {
			visibility: hidden;
		}
		.print-only, .print-only * {
			visibility: visible;
		}
		.print-only {
			display: block !important;
			position: absolute;
			left: 0;
			top: 0;
			width: 100%;
			background: #fff;
			color: #000;
			padding: 20px;
		}
	}
</style>

<script is:inline>
	// Standard Size Chart in Inches
	const sizeChartInches = [
		{ street: '00', bridal: 2, bust: 32.0, waist: 24.0, hip: 34.5 },
		{ street: '0',  bridal: 4, bust: 33.0, waist: 25.0, hip: 35.5 },
		{ street: '2',  bridal: 6, bust: 34.0, waist: 26.0, hip: 36.5 },
		{ street: '4',  bridal: 8, bust: 35.5, waist: 27.5, hip: 38.0 },
		{ street: '6',  bridal: 10, bust: 36.5, waist: 28.5, hip: 39.5 },
		{ street: '8',  bridal: 12, bust: 38.0, waist: 30.0, hip: 41.0 },
		{ street: '10', bridal: 14, bust: 39.5, waist: 31.5, hip: 42.5 },
		{ street: '12', bridal: 16, bust: 41.5, waist: 33.5, hip: 44.5 },
		{ street: '14', bridal: 18, bust: 43.5, waist: 35.5, hip: 46.5 },
		{ street: '16', bridal: 20, bust: 45.5, waist: 37.5, hip: 48.5 },
		{ street: '18', bridal: 22, bust: 47.5, waist: 39.5, hip: 50.5 },
		{ street: '20', bridal: 24, bust: 49.5, waist: 41.5, hip: 52.5 },
		{ street: '22', bridal: 26, bust: 52.0, waist: 44.0, hip: 55.0 },
		{ street: '24', bridal: 28, bust: 54.5, waist: 46.5, hip: 57.5 },
		{ street: '26', bridal: 30, bust: 57.0, waist: 49.0, hip: 60.0 }
	];

	let currentUnit = 'in'; // 'in' or 'cm'

	const bustInput = document.getElementById('input-bust');
	const waistInput = document.getElementById('input-waist');
	const hipsInput = document.getElementById('input-hips');
	const designerSelect = document.getElementById('input-designer');

	const resStreet = document.getElementById('res-street-size');
	const resBridal = document.getElementById('res-bridal-size');
	const resBodyShape = document.getElementById('res-body-shape');
	const resShapeDesc = document.getElementById('res-shape-desc');

	const barStreet = document.getElementById('bar-street');
	const barBridal = document.getElementById('bar-bridal');
	const barLabelStreet = document.getElementById('bar-label-street');
	const barLabelBridal = document.getElementById('bar-label-bridal');
	const sizeDiffNote = document.getElementById('size-diff-note');

	const matrixUs = document.getElementById('matrix-us');
	const matrixUk = document.getElementById('matrix-uk');
	const matrixEu = document.getElementById('matrix-eu');
	const matrixAu = document.getElementById('matrix-au');
	const matrixIt = document.getElementById('matrix-it');

	const alterationText = document.getElementById('alteration-advice-text');
	const silhouetteContainer = document.getElementById('silhouette-cards-container');

	function toInches(val) {
		return currentUnit === 'cm' ? val / 2.54 : val;
	}

	function calculateSizing() {
		let rawB = parseFloat(bustInput.value) || 36;
		let rawW = parseFloat(waistInput.value) || 28;
		let rawH = parseFloat(hipsInput.value) || 39;

		const bIn = toInches(rawB);
		const wIn = toInches(rawW);
		const hIn = toInches(rawH);

		// Find size for each measurement
		let bustSizeObj = sizeChartInches.find(s => bIn <= s.bust) || sizeChartInches[sizeChartInches.length - 1];
		let waistSizeObj = sizeChartInches.find(s => wIn <= s.waist) || sizeChartInches[sizeChartInches.length - 1];
		let hipSizeObj = sizeChartInches.find(s => hIn <= s.hip) || sizeChartInches[sizeChartInches.length - 1];

		// Maximum size needed to fit largest measurement
		const maxBridalSize = Math.max(bustSizeObj.bridal, waistSizeObj.bridal, hipSizeObj.bridal);
		const matchedObj = sizeChartInches.find(s => s.bridal === maxBridalSize) || sizeChartInches[sizeChartInches.length - 1];

		// Designer adjustments
		let adjustedBridal = maxBridalSize;
		const designer = designerSelect.value;
		if (designer === 'couture') {
			adjustedBridal = Math.min(30, maxBridalSize + 2); // runs small
		} else if (designer === 'davids') {
			adjustedBridal = Math.max(2, maxBridalSize - 2); // runs true to street
		}

		const streetSizeVal = matchedObj.street;

		// Determine Body Shape Archetype
		let shape = 'Hourglass';
		let shapeDetail = 'Balanced bust & hips with defined waist';
		let silhouettes = [
			{ name: 'Mermaid / Trumpet', desc: 'Highlights curves and naturally balanced proportions.' },
			{ name: 'Classic A-Line', desc: 'Universally flattering cinch at natural waistline.' }
		];

		if (hIn >= bIn + 2 && (hIn - wIn) >= 8) {
			shape = 'Pear / Triangle';
			shapeDetail = 'Hips wider than bust with smaller waist';
			silhouettes = [
				{ name: 'Ballgown / Princess', desc: 'Voluminous skirt skims easily over hips while highlighting waist.' },
				{ name: 'Empire / Flowing A-Line', desc: 'Draws focus upward to neckline and bodice.' }
			];
		} else if (bIn >= hIn + 2) {
			shape = 'Inverted Triangle';
			shapeDetail = 'Fuller bust / broader shoulders than hips';
			silhouettes = [
				{ name: 'A-Line with V-Neck', desc: 'Elongates torso and balances shoulder-to-hip ratio.' },
				{ name: 'Ballgown with Box Pleats', desc: 'Adds volume to lower half for perfect symmetry.' }
			];
		} else if (Math.abs(bIn - hIn) <= 2 && (bIn - wIn) <= 6) {
			shape = 'Rectangle / Athletic';
			shapeDetail = 'Uniform measurements with slight waist curve';
			silhouettes = [
				{ name: 'Fit-and-Flare', desc: 'Creates the optical illusion of curves at hips and bust.' },
				{ name: 'Corset Bodice Gown', desc: 'Defines waist structure with built-in boning.' }
			];
		}

		// Update UI
		resStreet.textContent = `US ${streetSizeVal}`;
		resBridal.textContent = `US ${adjustedBridal}`;
		resBodyShape.textContent = shape;
		resShapeDesc.textContent = shapeDetail;

		// Progress Comparison Bars
		const maxScale = 30;
		const streetNum = parseInt(streetSizeVal) || 6;
		const streetPct = Math.min(100, Math.round((streetNum / maxScale) * 100));
		const bridalPct = Math.min(100, Math.round((adjustedBridal / maxScale) * 100));

		barStreet.style.width = `${streetPct}%`;
		barBridal.style.width = `${bridalPct}%`;
		barLabelStreet.textContent = `US ${streetSizeVal}`;
		barLabelBridal.textContent = `US ${adjustedBridal}`;

		const diff = adjustedBridal - streetNum;
		sizeDiffNote.textContent = diff > 0 ? `+${diff} Sizes Up from Street` : 'Runs Close to Street Size';

		// International Matrix
		matrixUs.textContent = `${adjustedBridal}`;
		matrixUk.textContent = `${adjustedBridal + 2}`; // UK is +2 of US
		matrixEu.textContent = `${adjustedBridal + 30}`; // EU 40 for US 10
		matrixAu.textContent = `${adjustedBridal + 2}`; // AU is same as UK
		matrixIt.textContent = `${adjustedBridal + 34}`; // IT 44 for US 10

		// Alteration Advice Note
		let anchor = 'hips';
		if (bustSizeObj.bridal >= waistSizeObj.bridal && bustSizeObj.bridal >= hipSizeObj.bridal) anchor = 'bust';
		else if (waistSizeObj.bridal >= bustSizeObj.bridal && waistSizeObj.bridal >= hipSizeObj.bridal) anchor = 'waist';

		alterationText.innerHTML = `
			Your largest measurement is your <strong>${anchor} (Size ${maxBridalSize})</strong>. Order <strong>Size ${adjustedBridal}</strong> so the gown zips with ease. Your bridal seamstress can easily take in the remaining areas during standard fittings.
		`;

		// Silhouettes
		silhouetteContainer.innerHTML = '';
		silhouettes.forEach(s => {
			const div = document.createElement('div');
			div.className = 'silhouette-card';
			div.innerHTML = `
				<h5>✨ ${s.name}</h5>
				<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 0.85rem; margin: 0; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--fg-pencil);">${s.desc}</p>
			`;
			silhouetteContainer.appendChild(div);
		});
	}

	// Unit Switcher
	document.getElementById('unit-in').addEventListener('click', () => {
		if (currentUnit === 'in') return;
		currentUnit = 'in';
		document.getElementById('unit-in').classList.add('active-unit');
		document.getElementById('unit-cm').classList.remove('active-unit');
		document.querySelectorAll('.unit-label').forEach(el => el.textContent = 'inches');

		bustInput.value = (parseFloat(bustInput.value) / 2.54).toFixed(1);
		waistInput.value = (parseFloat(waistInput.value) / 2.54).toFixed(1);
		hipsInput.value = (parseFloat(hipsInput.value) / 2.54).toFixed(1);
		calculateSizing();
	});

	document.getElementById('unit-cm').addEventListener('click', () => {
		if (currentUnit === 'cm') return;
		currentUnit = 'cm';
		document.getElementById('unit-cm').classList.add('active-unit');
		document.getElementById('unit-in').classList.remove('active-unit');
		document.querySelectorAll('.unit-label').forEach(el => el.textContent = 'cm');

		bustInput.value = (parseFloat(bustInput.value) * 2.54).toFixed(1);
		waistInput.value = (parseFloat(waistInput.value) * 2.54).toFixed(1);
		hipsInput.value = (parseFloat(hipsInput.value) * 2.54).toFixed(1);
		calculateSizing();
	});

	// Presets
	document.querySelectorAll('.preset-meas-btn').forEach(btn => {
		btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
			let b = parseFloat(btn.getAttribute('data-b'));
			let w = parseFloat(btn.getAttribute('data-w'));
			let h = parseFloat(btn.getAttribute('data-h'));

			if (currentUnit === 'cm') {
				b = (b * 2.54).toFixed(1);
				w = (w * 2.54).toFixed(1);
				h = (h * 2.54).toFixed(1);
			}

			bustInput.value = b;
			waistInput.value = w;
			hipsInput.value = h;
			calculateSizing();
		});
	});

	// Input listeners
	bustInput.addEventListener('input', calculateSizing);
	waistInput.addEventListener('input', calculateSizing);
	hipsInput.addEventListener('input', calculateSizing);
	designerSelect.addEventListener('change', calculateSizing);

	// 📝 Export Word (.doc)
	document.getElementById('btn-export-doc').addEventListener('click', () => {
		const rawB = bustInput.value;
		const rawW = waistInput.value;
		const rawH = hipsInput.value;
		const unit = currentUnit === 'in' ? 'inches' : 'cm';

		const html = `
			<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">
			<head>
				<meta charset="utf-8">
				<title>Bridal Sizing & Fitting Card</title>
				<style>
					body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; padding: 20px; }
					h1 { color: #2d2d2d; margin-bottom: 4px; }
					p { color: #555; font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 20px; }
					table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 10px; font-size: 13px; }
					th { background-color: #f2f2f2; border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 8px; text-align: left; }
					td { border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 8px; }
				</style>
			</head>
			<body>
				<h1>Manage.Wedding — Official Bridal Sizing & Measurement Card</h1>
				<p>Generated on ${new Date().toLocaleDateString()} | Ready for Boutique Stylist & Seamstress</p>
				
				<h3>Client Body Measurements:</h3>
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr><th>Measurement Area</th><th>Client Value</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr><td><strong>Bust</strong></td><td>${rawB} ${unit}</td><td>Measured over planned bridal undergarments</td></tr>
						<tr><td><strong>Waist</strong></td><td>${rawW} ${unit}</td><td>Measured at natural narrowest point</td></tr>
						<tr><td><strong>Hips</strong></td><td>${rawH} ${unit}</td><td>Measured at widest point across buttocks</td></tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>

				<h3 style="margin-top:20px;">Recommended Sizing Summary:</h3>
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr><th>Standard</th><th>Size</th><th>Details</th></tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr><td><strong>Recommended US Bridal</strong></td><td><strong>${resBridal.textContent}</strong></td><td>Ordered to fit largest measurement</td></tr>
						<tr><td><strong>Everyday Street Size</strong></td><td>${resStreet.textContent}</td><td>Normal ready-to-wear sizing</td></tr>
						<tr><td><strong>UK Bridal Size</strong></td><td>${matrixUk.textContent}</td><td>UK / Australia Standard</td></tr>
						<tr><td><strong>EU Bridal Size</strong></td><td>${matrixEu.textContent}</td><td>European Standard</td></tr>
						<tr><td><strong>Body Silhouette Archetype</strong></td><td>${resBodyShape.textContent}</td><td>${resShapeDesc.textContent}</td></tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>

				<p style="margin-top:20px; font-size:12px; color:#666;">Advisory: Always double-check the specific designer's size chart before ordering.</p>
			</body>
			</html>
		`;

		const blob = new Blob(['\ufeff', html], { type: 'application/msword' });
		const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
		const a = document.createElement('a');
		a.href = url;
		a.download = `Bridal_Fitting_Card_${new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)}.doc`;
		document.body.appendChild(a);
		a.click();
		document.body.removeChild(a);
		URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
	});

	// 🖨️ Export PDF / Print
	document.getElementById('btn-export-pdf').addEventListener('click', () => {
		const printDate = document.getElementById('print-date');
		const printMeasBody = document.getElementById('print-meas-body');
		const printRecSize = document.getElementById('print-rec-size');
		const printStreetSize = document.getElementById('print-street-size');
		const printBodyShape = document.getElementById('print-body-shape');
		const printAlterationNote = document.getElementById('print-alteration-note');

		printDate.textContent = new Date().toLocaleDateString();
		const unit = currentUnit === 'in' ? 'inches' : 'cm';

		printMeasBody.innerHTML = `
			<tr>
				<td style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 6px; font-weight:bold;">1. Bust</td>
				<td style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 6px; text-align:center;">${bustInput.value} ${unit}</td>
				<td style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 6px; text-align:center;">Over bra / undergarments</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 6px; font-weight:bold;">2. Natural Waist</td>
				<td style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 6px; text-align:center;">${waistInput.value} ${unit}</td>
				<td style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 6px; text-align:center;">Narrowest point of torso</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 6px; font-weight:bold;">3. Hips</td>
				<td style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 6px; text-align:center;">${hipsInput.value} ${unit}</td>
				<td style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 6px; text-align:center;">Widest buttocks curve</td>
			</tr>
		`;

		printRecSize.textContent = `${resBridal.textContent} (UK ${matrixUk.textContent} / EU ${matrixEu.textContent})`;
		printStreetSize.textContent = resStreet.textContent;
		printBodyShape.textContent = `${resBodyShape.textContent} (${resShapeDesc.textContent})`;
		printAlterationNote.textContent = alterationText.textContent;

		window.print();
	});

	// Initialize
	calculateSizing();
</script>
